# irsat.rgb  -  simulated infrared brightness temperature colormap
#
# Designed to match the classic McIDAS / cyclonicwx IR palette:
# very cold cloud tops (< 200 K) in magenta / purple, deep convection
# (200-215 K) in dark red, developing convection (215-230 K) in
# red/orange, tropospheric clouds (230-260 K) in yellow/green, and
# lower clouds / sea surface (260-305 K) as a gray ramp (darkest point
# near 288 K to emulate the reference image's black zone around 10 C).
# Warm surfaces (>305 K, typically land / desert daytime) then
# transition through tan to warm brown/sienna.
#
# Sized for 34 interior bins at 5 K spacing (150 to 320 K) plus
# extend='both' under/over.  36 colors total, picked 1:1 by
# build_discrete_cmap.
#
# Boundaries: every 5 K from 150 to 320 K (inclusive).
#
#   <150 K     magenta                (under, very cold cirrus)
#   150-200 K  pink -> purple -> dark (overshooting convective tops)
#   200-215 K  dark red -> red        (strong deep convection)
#   215-230 K  red -> orange -> yellow (moderate convection)
#   230-260 K  yellow -> green -> pale (low to mid clouds)
#   260-305 K  GRAY RAMP              (sea surface / low clouds;
#                                      darkest around 288 K)
#   305-320 K  tan -> brown           (warm land / desert surfaces)
#   >320 K     warm sienna            (over)
#
ncolors=36
#r   g   b
255 102 200
255  70 180
255  40 170
230  50 155
200  60 150
175  60 150
150  55 140
120  45 125
 90  35 105
 60  20  75
 35  10  45
 50   0   5
 80   0   0
120   0   0
170   0   0
210   5   0
240  35   0
255  75   0
255 120   0
255 170   0
255 220   0
255 255   0
200 230  50
120 200  80
200 225 210
225 230 225
215 215 215
165 165 165
105 105 105
 85  85  85
105 100  95
